[{:adr/authoritative_for ["gftd CLI GFTD_LLM_* advisor wiring" "qwen3.6-35b-a3b fleet serving restoration (gad :8091 + qwen-gad.gftd.ai + infer.models re-route)"], :adr/topic "bmc-gftd-llm-advisor-murakumo-wiring", :adr/related ["adr-2607021600" "adr-2607022100" "adr-2607162100" "adr-2607172600"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607172700-bmc-gftd-llm-advisor-murakumo-wiring", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-17", :adr/body "# ADR-2607172700: BMC gftd CLI \u306b murakumo LLM advisor \u3092\u914d\u7dda -- itonami \u304c qwen3.6 \u3067\u81ea\u5f8b\u7684\u306b canvas \u3092\u56de\u3059\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner /loop directive: \u300cflagship \u3092\u9032\u3081\u3066\u3001\u5b9f\u969b\u306b itonami \u304c\u56de\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b, \u307e\u305f itonami \u81ea\u8eab\u304c api.murakumo.cloud \u3067 qwen3.6 \u3092\u4f7f\u3063\u3066, \u81ea\u5f8b\u7684\u306b\u51e6\u7406, business model canvas \u3092\u56de\u3059\u3088\u3046\u306b\u300d)\n**Scope**: `70-tools/bmc/src/gftd/cli.cljc` (+ tests), murakumo fleet node `gad` (new systemd unit), Cloudflare DNS (gftd.ai zone), murakumo KV `infer.models`\n**Builds on**: ADR-2607021600 (gftd CLI/ReAct loop), ADR-2607022100 (llm-advisor seam), ADR-2607162100 (api.murakumo.cloud /v1/messages consumers)\n\n## Context\n\n`gftd.react/llm-advisor` (the LLM seam, docstring explicitly anticipating \u300cmurakumo text\u300d) existed but was\nnever wired into the CLI -- `react tick/loop` hardcoded the mock+gate advisor. Meanwhile the fleet's\nqwen3.6-35b-a3b registry entry claimed \u300cserving on head(gad)\u300d but the gad GPU head had been re-purposed\nto gemma4-26b (yukkuri critic, dedicated cloudflared-gemma tunnel), so api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages\nsilently answered as gemma regardless of the requested model.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. CLI wiring (nbb/:cljs block only; :clj compat block keeps gate-only behavior)\n\n`GFTD_LLM_URL` set \u2192 `cmd-react` composes `gate-aware-advisor` + `llm-advisor(llm-complete-fn)`,\nactor label `advisor:llm+gate`. `llm-complete-fn` = synchronous curl execFileSync (react/tick is a\nsync pipeline; js/fetch is async), accepts BOTH OpenAI (`choices[0].message.content`) and Anthropic\n(`content[].text`) response shapes, strips markdown fences (`strip-fences`), env:\n`GFTD_LLM_MODEL` (default qwen3.6-35b-a3b) / `GFTD_LLM_TOKEN` (optional Bearer) /\n`GFTD_LLM_MAX_TOKENS` (default 3000). `normalize-llm-proposal` keywordizes string\n`:canvas/id`/`:hyp/id`/`:proposal/action` (measured drift: qwen3.6 emits strings, gemma4 emits\nkeywords); validity judgment stays with the governor. Tests: 18 tests / 98 assertions green.\n\n### 2. qwen3.6 restoration on the fleet (non-disruptive)\n\n- gad (46GB Strix Halo): GPU/GTT cannot hold both gemma4-26b and qwen3.6 \u2192 added a SECOND\n  llama-server as systemd `llama-server-qwen.service`: CPU `-ngl 0`, port 8091, 12/32 threads,\n  `OOMScoreAdjust=900` (it can die, the gemma head must not), mmap weights (page-cache evictable).\n  Measured 37 tok/s prefill / 20.6 tok/s decode -- 4-7x Xavier's CUDA head. gemma head verified\n  unharmed after load and under qwen generation.\n- Published as https://qwen-gad.gftd.ai: new ingress on the existing gemma-gad tunnel\n  (c9365124-e308) + CNAME in gftd.ai zone via CF API (`gftd.cloudflare/CF_API`). NOTE: local\n  `cloudflared tunnel route dns` used the etzhayyim.com-scoped cert and created a junk record\n  `qwen-gad.gftd.ai.etzhayyim.com` -- deleted via API; don't use route-dns cross-zone.\n- KV re-route: `PUT api.murakumo.cloud/infer/models/qwen3.6-35b-a3b` endpoint \u2192\n  https://qwen-gad.gftd.ai/v1/chat/completions with an honest note about the gemma re-purpose that\n  broke the old claim. Verified: /v1/messages with model qwen3.6-35b-a3b now answers as\n  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Q4_K_M.gguf.\n\n### 3. Cloudflare 100s (524) finding -- why long BMC ticks use tailnet\n\nThe real BMC advisor prompt (~3.5k chars) makes qwen3.6 think+generate for ~125s > Cloudflare's\n100s non-streaming origin limit \u2192 524 HTML \u2192 JSON parse throw \u2192 advisor fail-safe []. Short\ngenerations (<100s) work fine through api.murakumo.cloud. Until the complete-fn learns SSE\nstreaming (follow-up), long ticks run with `GFTD_LLM_URL=http://100.82.98.110:8091/v1/chat/completions`\n(gad via tailnet, same model/server as the public route).\n\n### 4. First autonomous qwen3.6 canvas turn (evidence in canvas-ledger.edn seq 3673-3693)\n\nThe ledger records the full honest history: 0-proposal fail-safe observations (timeout/format),\n5 governor-REJECTED qwen proposals (string canvas ids, pre-normalization), then the landed turns --\ngemma-served tick (5 approved) and the genuine qwen3.6 tick (5 approved: checkout_completion_rate /\nstripe_webhook_success_rate instrumentation, paid-path channel pivot, probe-noise segmentation,\nper-seat + per-agent-run billing operationalization, decision-ledger accumulation-rate as unfair\nleading indicator). Model attribution per turn is stated here since the ledger's actor field\n(`advisor:llm+gate`) does not carry the model id (follow-up candidate).\n\n## Consequences / follow-ups\n\n- Any BMC product loop can now run LLM-advised via env -- no code change per product.\n- Follow-ups: SSE streaming in llm-complete-fn (lifts the 100s ceiling on the public path);\n  model id in ledger events; hourly routine (`itonami-react-growth-hourly`) can adopt\n  GFTD_LLM_* once an operator decides the cost/latency budget.\n- kagi checkout staleness (local 2026-07-04; `MURAKUMO_CRITIC_TOKEN` in the secrets map but absent\n  locally) noted -- token was read from 1Password instead (`gftd.murakumo/ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN`,\n  by item UUID because the title contains a slash).\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-17", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607172700: BMC gftd CLI murakumo LLM advisor wiring -- itonami autonomous canvas turns on qwen3.6", :adr/source-format "edn"}]